<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_centering">
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Material 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Token Importance Analysis</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The method for calculating token importance described in this section is adapted from the Zero-TPrune model proposed by Wang et al. It is important to note that Zero-TPrune was originally designed for the <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">visual domain</span>, where it analyzes the attention graph to calculate the importance of <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">image</span> patches (also treated as tokens) for pruning Vision Transformers. In this study, we migrate and apply this methodology from the visual domain to the <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">textual domain</span>, aiming to quantify the semantic importance of each text token within a natural language context.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The method consists of two main components:</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Weighted PageRank (WPR) Algorithm</span>: Used to calculate token importance scores within a single attention head.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Head Score Fusion Strategy</span>: Combines a Variance-based Head Filter (VHF) and Emphasizing Informative Region (EIR) aggregation to fuse scores from multiple heads.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Single-Head Importance via Weighted PageRank</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The WPR algorithm treats the attention matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> from a single attention head as the adjacency matrix of a weighted directed graph. It iteratively calculates the importance score of each node (i.e., token) in the graph. The importance of a token is determined by the weighted importance of other tokens that point to it. The calculation process is shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.1 Single-Head Importance via Weighted PageRank ‣ Appendix A Token Importance Analysis ‣ Guiding Diffusion Models with Semantically Degraded Conditions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> PageRank for Token Importance Scoring</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Attention matrix <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, token length <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Convergence threshold <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum iterations <math id="alg1.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0b" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0b.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Token importance scores <math id="alg1.l0b.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\text{row\_norm}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>row_norm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\text{row\_norm}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             Initialize uniform importance scores <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(0)}=\frac{1}{n}\mathbf{1}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(0)}=\frac{1}{n}\mathbf{1}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> iteration <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{prev}=s^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{prev}=s^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(t)}=A^{T}s^{prev}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(t)}=A^{T}s^{prev}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(t)}=s^{(t)}/\|s^{(t)}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(t)}=s^{(t)}/\|s^{(t)}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s^{(t)}-s^{prev}\|_{1}&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s^{(t)}-s^{prev}\|_{1}&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Multi-Head Score Fusion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a multi-head attention mechanism, after obtaining an independent score distribution from each head via the WPR algorithm, these scores must be fused into a final score. A simple averaging of scores is not optimal, as different heads may focus on different semantic patterns. The method employs a fusion strategy that combines a Variance-based Head Filter (VHF) and Emphasizing Informative Region (EIR) aggregation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variance-based Head Filter (VHF):</span> This technique is used to identify and filter out ”bad” heads that provide uninformative or misleading score distributions. The procedure involves calculating the variance, <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, of the importance score distribution for each head. Only heads whose variance falls within a predefined threshold range [<math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\min},v_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\min},v_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>] are retained; the rest are discarded from subsequent calculations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Emphasizing Informative Region (EIR):</span> For the valid heads filtered by VHF, this method uses a ”root-mean of sum of squares” approach for score aggregation. Compared to a direct average, the squaring operation amplifies high scores from any single head. This ensures that a token’s high importance is not diluted in the final score, even if it is deemed critical by only a few ”specialist” heads.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final Score Calculation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the VHF and EIR strategies, the final importance score <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(l)}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(l)}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for the <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token in the <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer is calculated as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(l)}\left(x_{i}\right)=\sqrt{\frac{\sum_{h=1}^{N_{h}}s^{(h,l)}\left(x_{i}\right)^{2}\cdot\eta\left(v_{\min}\leq\mathrm{Var}_{h}\leq v_{\max}\right)}{\sum_{h=1}^{N_{h}}\eta\left(v_{\min}\leq\mathrm{Var}_{h}\leq v_{\max}\right)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(l)}\left(x_{i}\right)=\sqrt{\frac{\sum_{h=1}^{N_{h}}s^{(h,l)}\left(x_{i}\right)^{2}\cdot\eta\left(v_{\min}\leq\mathrm{Var}_{h}\leq v_{\max}\right)}{\sum_{h=1}^{N_{h}}\eta\left(v_{\min}\leq\mathrm{Var}_{h}\leq v_{\max}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Where:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(h,l)}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(h,l)}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the importance score of token <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from head <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> in layer <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance of the score distribution for head <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is an indicator function that implements the VHF. The function returns 1 if the condition <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\min}\leq\mathrm{Var}_{h}\leq v_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\min}\leq\mathrm{Var}_{h}\leq v_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is met, and 0 otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of heads in the current layer.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Cross attention</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A natural baseline for computing token importance is to leverage the cross-attention mechanism between text and image tokens. In diffusion models, the cross-attention matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{\text{img}}\times N_{\text{text}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{\text{img}}\times N_{\text{text}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed where image tokens serve as queries and text tokens serve as keys. For each text token <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, its attention weights across all image positions form the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th column of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. These weights are typically reshaped to the spatial dimensions of the latent to produce saliency maps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following this intuition, one might compute the importance score of text token <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> by simply summing its corresponding column:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{\text{cross}}=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{img}}}C_{j,i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>cross</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub></munderover><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{\text{cross}}=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{img}}}C_{j,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, this approach yields counterintuitive results. Consider the prompt “A man is cooking, Minecraft Style.” As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ A.3 Cross attention ‣ Appendix A Token Importance Analysis ‣ Guiding Diffusion Models with Semantically Degraded Conditions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, the cross-attention-based importance scores assign the highest values predominantly to padding tokens, rather than to semantically meaningful tokens like “man”, “cooking”, or “Minecraft”. This paradoxical behavior contradicts our intuition and renders cross-attention unsuitable for token importance estimation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.10780v1/token_importance.svg" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:651/191;" width="651" height="191"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A1.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Token importance scores computed via cross-attention summation for the prompt “A man is cooking, Minecraft Style.” The method incorrectly assigns highest importance to padding tokens rather than semantic content tokens.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This failure motivates our graph-based approach using self-attention and Weighted PageRank, which properly captures token relationships and avoids the padding token bias inherent in cross-attention aggregation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the complete algorithmic and implementation details of our Condition-Degradation Guidance (CDG). We present: (1) the full sampling algorithm that integrates CDG into the diffusion denoising loop, and (2) the core PyTorch implementation for token degradation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Algorithm: CDG Sampling</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Main Sampling Loop ‣ B.1 Algorithm: CDG Sampling ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Guiding Diffusion Models with Semantically Degraded Conditions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> details the complete CDG sampling procedure, which augments the standard diffusion sampling loop with our semantic degradation mechanism. The algorithm consists of three key components:</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CalculateImportance</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(lines 2–7) computes token importance scores using the Weighted PageRank (WPR) algorithm on the self-attention graph. It extracts the attention affinity matrix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}</annotation></semantics></math> from transformer block <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{block}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>block</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{block}}</annotation></semantics></math>, applies WPR and multi-head fusion, and returns sorted token indices <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{i}_{\text{sorted}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒊</mi><mtext>sorted</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{i}_{\text{sorted}}</annotation></semantics></math> in descending order of importance. For efficiency, this is computed only once at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> and cached for all subsequent steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ProcessToken</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(lines 9–11) constructs the degraded condition <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}_{\text{deg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}_{\text{deg}}</annotation></semantics></math> at each timestep. Using the cached importance ranking and degradation ratios <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{deg}}=\{r_{\text{content}},r_{\text{CtxAgg}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>content</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>CtxAgg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{deg}}=\{r_{\text{content}},r_{\text{CtxAgg}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, it builds a binary mask <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{m}</annotation></semantics></math> that marks less important tokens for replacement, then performs masked interpolation: <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}_{\text{deg}}\leftarrow\boldsymbol{m}\odot\boldsymbol{c}+(1-\boldsymbol{m})\odot\boldsymbol{c}_{\emptyset}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒎</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝒄</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}_{\text{deg}}\leftarrow\boldsymbol{m}\odot\boldsymbol{c}+(1-\boldsymbol{m})\odot\boldsymbol{c}_{\emptyset}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Main Sampling Loop</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(lines 13–22) performs guided denoising for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps. At each timestep <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, it computes two noise predictions—<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> with full condition <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{deg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{deg}}</annotation></semantics></math> with degraded condition <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}_{\text{deg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}_{\text{deg}}</annotation></semantics></math>—then combines them via the CDG formula: <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}\leftarrow\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{cond}}+(w-1)\cdot(\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{cond}}-\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{deg}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}\leftarrow\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{cond}}+(w-1)\cdot(\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{cond}}-\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{\text{deg}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is the guidance scale.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Sampling with Condition-Degradation Guidance (CDG)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
                
                
               Initial noise <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\boldsymbol{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\boldsymbol{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, text embedding <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, empty embedding <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}_{\emptyset}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}_{\emptyset}</annotation></semantics></math>, guidance scale <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, denoising steps <math id="alg2.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, denoiser <math id="alg2.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, transformer block index <math id="alg2.l0.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{block}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>block</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{block}}</annotation></semantics></math>, degradation ratio <math id="alg2.l0.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{deg}}=\{r_{\text{content}},r_{\text{CtxAgg}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>deg</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>content</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>CtxAgg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{deg}}=\{r_{\text{content}},r_{\text{CtxAgg}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
                
                
               Generated image <math id="alg2.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
